  "notes": "Nursing home (Wisner Care Center, a component unit of the City of Wisner), accrual basis, entirely business-type; governmental fields null. Trimmed PDF (find_pages v8): Statement of Net Position (p1, report p11), Statement of Revenues, Expenses, and Changes in Net Position (p2, report p12, added by the v8 re-trim), Statement of Cash Flows (p3, report p13) and Operating Expenditures by Department pie charts (p4, report p29; percentages only, no dollar amounts, so not recorded in detail). Receipts/disbursements from p2, 2025 Amount column only (per-inpatient-day and 2024 columns ignored). Direct cost of services and administrative expense lines each recorded as disbursements (hospital/health care). Quality assurance assessment (102,411) and interest expense (18,114) are printed among nonoperating revenues (expenses) but recorded as disbursements; negative nonoperating items Uncollectible ERC (189,411), Loss on disposal (82,770) and ARPA grant (78,459) kept as negative receipts. Receipts check: operating 3,672,102 - 189,411 + 836 + 47,881 - 82,770 - 78,459 + 4,124 = 3,374,303; disbursements 3,797,051 + 309,851 + 102,411 + 18,114 = 4,227,427; net (853,124) = printed decrease in net position; 1,643,317 -> 790,193 ties. Contract services - Stanton and DHHS van grant are dashes for 2025, not recorded. No detail schedules. proprietary values are the total (only) column of the cash flow statement (p3); there is no noncapital financing section. Cash flow statement cash 236,468 -> 825,114 ties. Balance sheet balances (1,775,750 = 985,557 + 790,193). Resident cash 3,110 shown as restricted assets and matching resident funds liability. Zero lines (construction in progress, ERC receivable, unearned grant advance, restricted for awning project) not recorded. Read pages 1-4 of 4",
